---
// Refund policy. Prices come from pricing.yaml; keep this consistent with /terms section 5 and the
// pricing FAQ, which both point here for the exceptions.
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { pricing, site } from '../config';
import { billingLabel, formatPrice } from '../lib/format';

const email = site.supportEmail;
const tier = (id: string) => pricing.tiers.find((t) => t.id === id)!;
const plan = tier('self-hosted');
const addOn = pricing.addOn;
const setup = pricing.setup;
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Refund policy"
  description="When the PACSinfra plan, the add-on and renewals can be refunded, and how to ask for a refund."
  updated="24 October 2026"
  draft={false}
>
  <p>PACSinfra is sold as source code. Once you have the code, it cannot be “returned”, so the policy is simple and strict. Please read it before buying.</p>

  <h2>{plan.name} ({formatPrice(plan.price)} {billingLabel(plan.billing)})</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Before the source code is delivered:</strong> full refund on request.</li>
    <li><strong>After that:</strong> no refund, except where required by law.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Before you buy, you can:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>try the live demo at <a href={site.demoUrl}>demo.pacsinfra.com</a>, which runs the same software (some features are turned off there);</li>
    <li>email me with questions about whether it fits your use case. I would rather answer them than process a refund request.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If you paid but have not yet received the download link or repository access, email me and I will cancel the order and refund in full.</p>

  <h2>{setup.name} (+{formatPrice(setup.price)})</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Before setup work starts:</strong> full refund on request.</li>
    <li><strong>After it starts:</strong> no refund, except that if I cannot complete the setup for reasons on my side (not caused by your infrastructure, access delays or scope changes), I will refund the setup in full.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>{addOn.name} (+{formatPrice(addOn.price)})</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Before the add-on work starts:</strong> full refund on request.</li>
    <li><strong>After it starts:</strong> no refund, except that if I cannot complete it for reasons on my side, I will refund the add-on in full.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Maintenance renewals</h2>
  <p>Full refund if requested within 14 days of the renewal payment and you have not opened a support request in that period. After that, no refund; the renewal runs for its full 12 months.</p>

  <h2>Data migration, integration and custom development</h2>
  <p>Covered by the individual quote. In general, deposits are non-refundable once work begins, and completed milestones are not refundable.</p>

  <h2>Mistakes and duplicates</h2>
  <p>Duplicate payments, the wrong item ordered, or a purchase made in error that you report before receiving the download link or repository access: refunded in full, no questions asked.</p>

  <h2>How to request a refund</h2>
  <p>Email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> with your invoice number. I reply within 2 business days (Taiwan time). Refunds are paid by bank transfer to the account the payment came from, normally within 10 business days of the refund being agreed.</p>

  <h2>Legal</h2>
  <p>Nothing here limits refund rights you have under mandatory consumer law in your country. Where that law applies and conflicts with this policy, the law wins.</p>
</LegalLayout>
